        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fb2b6dda-9dd1-55f1-9052-338a1701f4d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Cercle Proudhon\n- People: Pierre-Joseph Proudhon, George Valois, Édouard Berth, Georges Sorel\n- Works: What Is Property?\n- Concepts: Mutualism, federalism, anarchist philosophy, property\n- Places: France\n\nFacts:\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was born on 15 January 1809 and died on 19 January 1865.\n- In 1840, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon first published What Is Property?, a nonfiction work about property and its relation to anarchist philosophy.\n- After the French Revolution of 1848, Pierre-Joseph Proudhon became a member of the French Parliament and thereafter described himself as a federalist.\n- Pierre-Joseph Proudhon was a French politician and the founder of mutualist philosophy.\n- Cercle Proudhon was founded in France on 16 December 1911 by George Valois and Édouard Berth.\n- Cercle Proudhon was inspired by Georges Sorel and by a selective reading of Pierre-Joseph Proudhon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4a224775-6507-577c-9a46-9f09ec0c2321",
        "text": "Page: Cercle Proudhon. Sentence: Cercle Proudhon (Circle Proudhon) was a political group founded in France on December 16, 1911 by George Valois and Édouard Berth.\nPage: Cercle Proudhon. Sentence: The group was inspired by Georges Sorel and a selective reading of Proudhon.\nPage: Pierre-Joseph Proudhon. Sentence: Pierre-Joseph Proudhon (] ; 15 January 1809 – 19 January 1865) was a French politician and the founder of mutualist philosophy.\nPage: Pierre-Joseph Proudhon. Sentence: He became a member of the French Parliament after the revolution of 1848, whereafter he referred to himself as a federalist.\nPage: What Is Property?. Sentence: ou Recherche sur le principe du Droit et du Gouvernement\" ) is a work of nonfiction on the concept of property and its relation to anarchist philosophy by the French anarchist and mutualist Pierre-Joseph Proudhon, first published in 1840.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
